    "body": "Updates `hydra-core` to address GHSA-2cp2-2r3c-7p7r, GHSA-c3wx-c55w-pxjq, and PYSEC-2026-3850.\n\nEvidence:\n- `pyproject.toml` pinned `hydra-core==1.3.2` in the `gpu` and `xpu` extras\n- OSV reports GHSA-2cp2-2r3c-7p7r, GHSA-c3wx-c55w-pxjq, and PYSEC-2026-3850 for 1.3.2\n- 1.3.6 is the minimal fix for those three but still falls in range for GHSA-mwj6-rfh8-7qf4, so this jumps to 1.3.7, the lowest version clear of all current advisories\n- updated version: `1.3.7`\n\nValidation:\n- OSV reports no advisories for `hydra-core@1.3.7`\n- 1.3.7 dependency metadata is unchanged (`omegaconf<2.4,>=2.2`, `antlr4-python3-runtime==4.9.*`, `packaging`), compatible with the repo's `omegaconf==2.3.0` pin and `requires-python = \">=3.10\"`\n- `pip download --no-deps hydra-core==1.3.7` succeeds\n\nScope: dependency pin update in `pyproject.toml` only.\n\nCommit author katsugtgz, unsigned.\n",
